ther login, another tab, another interruption.\n\nThe daily summary closes that gap. Every morning, a clear snapshot of your open tickets arrives where your team already works, so everyone starts the day on the same page.\n\n## What's in each summary\n\nPosted at the time you choose, each digest includes:\n\n- **Total open tickets**, broken down by priority\n- **Unassigned tickets** that still need an owner\n- **Tickets awaiting a response**, so nothing goes stale\n- **Your oldest open ticket**, because aging issues shouldn't hide\n- **A direct link** to jump straight into the full queue\n\nOne message. Ten seconds to read. A complete picture of the day ahead.\n\n## Set up in under two minutes\n\n1. Go to **Settings → Integrations → Slack**\n2. Click **Connect to Slack** and authorize your workspace\n3. Pick your channel and delivery time\n4. Save — your first summary arrives tomorrow morning\n\nNo admin approval workflows, no configuration files, no downtime.\n\n## A few ways teams are using it\n\n- **Support leads** post summaries to their team channel each morning to kick off triage\n- **Engineering teams** follow the support channel to spot bug reports trending upward\n- **Executives** get visibility into support health without asking for a report\n\n## Available today\n\nThe Slack integration is live now for all customers, on every plan, at no additional cost.\n\n**Ready to try it?**\n\n[Connect Slack now →] | [Read the setup guide →]\n\nAs always, we'd love your feedback — tell us what you'd like to see in future summaries at [support email].\n\nHere's to fewer surprises hiding in the queue.\n\n— The [Product Name] Team\n\n---\n\n*Word count: ~360. Placeholders in brackets — product name, links, and contact email — can be swapped in before publishing. Happy to adjust the tone (more formal, more playful), trim it for email format, or add a FAQ section if helpful.*\n=== END OF TEXT A ===\n\n=== TEXT B ===\n## New: Daily Open Ticket Summaries in Slack\n\nKeeping 